    "evidence_text": "North Irvington Gardens Historic District\n\nHistoric Inner East, Dayton, Ohio\n\nThe Historic Inner East neighborhood is located in Dayton, Ohio, United States.\n\n The neighborhood boundaries include two historic districts: Saint Anne's Hill Historic District and Huffman Historic District.\n\nCenter Street Historic District (Ashland, Ohio)\n\n The Center Street Historic District Association is the homeowners' association for the district.\n\nCentral Avenue Historic District (Dayton, Ohio)\n\nHuffman Historic District\n\nThe Huffman Historic District is a historic neighborhood in eastern Dayton, Ohio, United States.\n\nSaint Anne's Hill Historic District\n\nSaint Anne's Hill Historic District is part of the Historic Inner East neighborhood in Dayton, Ohio, United States.\n\n The neighborhood is significant for its German heritage.\n\nTorrence Huffman\n\nTorrence Huffman was a banker in Dayton, Ohio who loaned pasture land to the Wright brothers where they perfected their first airplanes and started the first pilot training school.\n\nEast Windsor Hill Historic District\n\n It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1986.\n\n The district is located directly north of another historic district, Windsor Farms Historic District.\n\nEast Walnut Hills, Cincinnati\n\nEast Walnut Hills is a neighborhood in Cincinnati, Ohio, United States.\n\nSwiss Avenue Historic District",
